# NVMe devices have deep hardware queues and do their own reordering, so an
# extra kernel I/O scheduler mostly adds CPU work and latency. `none` is the
# usual recommendation for NVMe; this box was on mq-deadline.
#
# Effect is modest and I have not benchmarked it on this machine - it is a
# best-practice default, not a measured win. Delete this file to revert.
ACTION=="add|change", KERNEL=="nvme[0-9]n[0-9]", ATTR{queue/scheduler}="none"
